+{
+  "decision": "request-changes",
+  "rationale": "Three lenses converge on a shared class of defect: the PoC test module does not sufficiently isolate the fuzzer from real side effects. (a) Path-exclusion regex misses 6+ LLM/generation endpoints (generate, refine, prompt/generate, virtual/model, {id}/model, slug/{}/model) and the /mcp/test endpoint, so the safety net for AC-4 (\"no external LLM calls happen\") depends on LiteLLM not being configured in the runtime environment — fragile. (b) No DB transactional isolation: fuzz-generated POST/PUT/DELETE reach the real local DB (the Class A crash in findings.md proves live DB traffic). (c) app.router.lifespan_context mutation persists for the pytest session, contaminating other router tests. (d) ENV=local via os.environ.setdefault is silently ignored if ENV is pre-set to something else. (e) The dev-dep (schemathesis) is not in pyproject.toml/lock, so a fresh checkout cannot collect the module — a known trade-off per user decision (codemie-enterprise registry auth) but still blocks reproducibility and must be tracked. Six blocking findings recorded (3 critical, 3 major); other lens outputs classified as defer/dismiss. Confidence high — the findings replicate across independent lenses.",
+  "confidence": "high",
+  "risk_flags": ["security", "cost"],
+  "business_review": [
+    {"id": "AC-1", "criterion": "Suite executes end-to-end via from_asgi with max_examples=30 and produces JUnit XML", "status": "partial", "notes": "Suite ran locally (426s, 49 endpoints, JUnit XML produced). Fresh checkout cannot reproduce because dev-dep is not committed (see CR-004)."},
+    {"id": "AC-2", "criterion": "A check failure fails pytest with endpoint + input in the report", "status": "pass", "notes": "red-baseline.txt lists 42 endpoint-scoped FAILED IDs; findings.md Class A includes a full reproducer curl."},
+    {"id": "AC-3", "criterion": "user-id header ENV=local bypass carries auth on every request; no 401 noise", "status": "pass", "notes": "7 endpoints PASSed → auth reached handlers. But CR-005 makes this fragile if ENV is pre-set."},
+    {"id": "AC-4", "criterion": "LLM/agent/enterprise routes excluded via path regex; no external LLM calls happen", "status": "fail", "notes": "See CR-001: 6+ LLM-invoking endpoints slip past the exclusion regex. CR-002: /assistants/mcp/test not excluded either. In this specific run no LLM calls succeeded only because LiteLLM was unconfigured (lifespan stubbed) — the AC's guarantee is not actually enforced by the filter."},
+    {"id": "AC-5", "criterion": "Runs as separate CI stage, not in pre-commit", "status": "deferred", "notes": "Per spec, CI wiring is out-of-band in the external devops repo."},
+    {"id": "AC-6", "criterion": "Schemathesis stage is isolated from other test modules", "status": "partial", "notes": "Structurally in its own module, but CR-006 leaks lifespan mutation into any other test module that reuses the app object in the same pytest session."},
+    {"id": "AC-7", "criterion": "Go/no-go decision recorded in the ticket after first meaningful run", "status": "partial", "notes": "Verdict committed to findings.md in the branch. Not yet posted as a Jira ticket comment on EPMCDME-13772 — follow-up handoff task, not a code-review blocker."},
+    {"id": "SPEC-SIGNAL", "criterion": "Success signal: >=3 distinct classes of findings", "status": "pass", "notes": "3 empirically-confirmed classes (A empty-DB unpack, B MCP loader, C MagicMock leak) + 1 latent (D error-envelope drift). Threshold met on confirmed alone. Consider distinguishing production vs test-infra in the Jira comment."}
+  ],
+  "standards_review": [
+    {"standard": "commit message format (git-workflow.md)", "status": "pass", "notes": "Commits use conventional-commit style with ticket ref (EPMCDME-13772)."},
+    {"standard": "Apache 2.0 license header (code-quality.md)", "status": "pass", "notes": "test_schemathesis_assistants.py carries the standard EPAM header copied from sibling test files."},
+    {"standard": "security-patterns.md — no external side effects in tests", "status": "fail", "notes": "See CR-001, CR-002, CR-003. Fuzzer can trigger real network + DB writes; violates the test-isolation baseline the security guide implies."}
+  ],
+  "findings": [
+    {
+      "id": "CR-001",
+      "severity": "critical",
+      "triage": "patch",
+      "category": "security / spec-compliance",
+      "problem": "Path exclusion regex (?i)(chat|agent|evaluate|ask|enterprise) does not match LLM-invoking endpoints in the assistants router: /assistants/generate, /assistants/refine, /assistants/prompt/generate, /assistants/virtual/model, /assistants/{assistant_id}/model, /assistants/slug/{slug}/model.",
+      "impact": "Violates AC-4 (\"no external LLM calls happen\"). In an environment where LiteLLM is configured (a CI runner with real credentials, or a future improvement to lifespan mocking that wires LiteLLM), the fuzzer will emit real LLM API calls with random prompts — token cost, rate-limit exposure, and semantic noise in findings.",
+      "recommendation": "Extend the exclude regex to explicitly cover 'generate', 'refine', 'model' as full path segments (e.g. add /generate$|/refine$|/model$|/model/|/mcp_tools). Prefer segment-anchored regex (`/generate\\b`) over substring match so future endpoint names named around these tokens are still fuzzed. Add a comment in the test file cross-referencing this finding and the list of intentionally-excluded endpoint families.",
+      "sources": ["edge-case", "blind"]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "CR-002",
+      "severity": "critical",
+      "triage": "patch",
+      "category": "security",
+      "problem": "POST /assistants/mcp/test is not excluded. The MCP tester makes a live outbound network call to the URL in the request body. Schemathesis will feed it arbitrary URLs from the OpenAPI schema's string generator.",
+      "impact": "SSRF probe surface: fuzzer-generated URLs can point at localhost, internal metadata endpoints, or arbitrary external hosts. Real outbound traffic per fuzz example.",
+      "recommendation": "Add /mcp/test (and any other endpoint whose contract is 'call an external URL') to the path-exclude regex. Same fix as CR-001.",
+      "sources": ["edge-case"]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "CR-003",
+      "severity": "critical",
+      "triage": "patch",
+      "category": "test-isolation / safety",
+      "problem": "The test module does not wrap fuzz-generated requests in a rolled-back DB transaction or a fixture-isolated test DB. Fuzz-generated POST /assistants, PUT /assistants/{id}, DELETE /assistants/{id}, category CRUD, marketplace publish, etc., reach the real local database.",
+      "impact": "Repeated runs pollute the local dev DB with fuzz artifacts. If the local DB is shared or points at staging (misconfiguration risk), real data could be corrupted or deleted. Run duration is also inflated by DB round-trips.",
+      "recommendation": "Wrap the test session in a transactional fixture (savepoint per case, rollback on teardown), OR require a disposable test DB via a pytest-managed fixture, OR limit the fuzz to read-only endpoints for the first iteration. Whichever route, the test must guarantee zero net DB mutation across the session.",
+      "sources": ["edge-case"]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "CR-004",
+      "severity": "major",
+      "triage": "decision_needed",
+      "category": "repro / build",
+      "problem": "`schemathesis` is not declared in pyproject.toml and not present in poetry.lock. The committed test file will fail at collection with `ModuleNotFoundError` on any fresh checkout, CI runner, or reviewer's machine that has not manually installed it into the poetry venv.",
+      "impact": "Test is effectively dead in CI and reviewer environments. The 'schemathesis runs as a separate CI stage' follow-up (AC-5) is blocked until the dep is committed.",
+      "recommendation": "This is a known trade-off per user decision (codemie-enterprise registry auth was unavailable). Two acceptable resolutions: (a) commit pyproject.toml with `schemathesis = \"~4.10\"` + regenerated lock in a follow-up MR from an environment that HAS the enterprise auth, and gate merge of this branch behind that follow-up; OR (b) guard the module with `schemathesis = pytest.importorskip('schemathesis')` at the top so collection degrades gracefully to SKIPPED rather than ERROR, with a module docstring linking the follow-up ticket.",
+      "sources": ["blind", "acceptance"]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "CR-005",
+      "severity": "major",
+      "triage": "patch",
+      "category": "correctness",
+      "problem": "`os.environ.setdefault(\"ENV\", \"local\")` only sets ENV if it is unset. If the pytest runner starts with ENV already exported to a non-'local' value (e.g., 'test', 'dev', a CI default), the setdefault is a no-op and the user-id header bypass in PersistentUserProvider is silently inactive.",
+      "impact": "All 49 test cases fail with 401/403 rather than surfacing real contract findings. The test appears to run (no framework error) but produces zero signal.",
+      "recommendation": "Change to `os.environ[\"ENV\"] = \"local\"` for the test module's scope, OR add an assertion `assert os.environ.get(\"ENV\") == \"local\"` at fixture-setup time that fails fast if the env was pre-set to something else. Log a one-line reason when overriding.",
+      "sources": ["blind", "edge-case"]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "CR-006",
+      "severity": "major",
+      "triage": "patch",
+      "category": "test-isolation",
+      "problem": "`app.router.lifespan_context = _noop_lifespan` mutates the shared module-level FastAPI `app` object at import time and never restores it. Any co-collected test that imports the same `app` (any other router test in the same pytest session) inherits the stubbed lifespan silently.",
+      "impact": "Other router tests that depend on lifespan-initialized state (IDP validator, LiteLLM client pool, Redis session cache) operate on uninitialized state → misleading failures or false passes. AC-6 (isolation) partially unmet.",
+      "recommendation": "Capture the original lifespan in a session-scoped fixture, monkeypatch inside a `yield`, and restore in teardown. Alternatively, deep-copy the app for the schemathesis module. Also add a `@pytest.mark.schemathesis` marker and document a dedicated `make test-schemathesis` target so this module is never accidentally swept into `pytest tests/`.",
+      "sources": ["blind", "edge-case"]
+    }
+  ]
+}
